MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello there Shiny users ...

I'm pretty sure that I'm just being dense, but completely unable to find the answer to this.

For our sets of data, we have roughly 4 "layers" of reactivity.  The first layer being the raw data, second layer is filters, third layer is groupings, and the final layer is the display formatting, etc.  With this, we are able to source the raw data for multiple views, and then the amount of processing is significantly reduced.

My problem is that I would like to create a withProgress function that encompasses all of these levels, so that I can have one progress bar and the ability to update that progress from all levels of reactivity.  With four levels of reactivity, we have four separate progress bars and it just looks bad.

The reason we need to have progress bars is because our data takes up to 30 seconds to load/process (on first load), so it leaves a lot up to the imagination if we don't include progress indicators, and WAY too much progress indicator if we do withProgress for all different pieces of reactive data.

Does anyone have any examples or suggestions for how this could be accomplished?

Any help would be greatly appreciated.  Thanks!
~Laz

